---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Project Two" description="A production-ready static site with minimal dependencies and fast load times.">
  <section class="max-w-2xl">
    <p class="mb-4 text-sm tracking-wide text-text-light">
      <a href="/projects" class="hover:text-primary">← Projects</a>
    </p>
    <h1 class="mb-4 text-3xl font-black text-text-dark md:text-5xl">Project Two</h1>
    <p class="mb-8 text-text-light">A production-ready static site with minimal dependencies and fast load times.</p>

    <img
      src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518773553398-650c184e0bb3?w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80"
      alt="Project Two"
      width="1200"
      height="630"
      class="mb-10 w-full rounded-lg object-cover"
      loading="eager"
    />

    <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl text-text-dark">Overview</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-text-light">
      Project Two is a production-ready static site engineered for reliability and speed. The brief was clear: ship
      something that loads fast on any connection, requires no backend, and can be maintained by a single developer
      without a framework upgrade cycle to worry about.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-10 text-text-light">
      The result is a site with a minimal dependency tree — Astro, Tailwind, and nothing else. No CMS, no build-time
      API calls, no client-side JavaScript unless strictly necessary.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl text-text-dark">What I built</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-text-light">
      Content is managed as flat Astro files, making edits straightforward without needing a CMS login or API token.
      A custom Tailwind theme enforces consistent spacing, colour, and type scale across every page.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-10 text-text-light">
      CI/CD is wired up through GitHub Actions: every push triggers a fresh build and deploy to GitHub Pages in under
      30 seconds, with zero downtime and automatic rollback on failure.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl text-text-dark">Tech stack</h2>
    <ul class="mb-10 list-disc pl-5 text-text-light space-y-1">
      <li>Astro</li>
      <li>Tailwind CSS</li>
      <li>TypeScript</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>
